meshforge is research-grade software. It is not a medical device, has not
been cleared or approved by any regulatory body, and must not be used for
diagnosis or treatment.

No patient data is contained in this repository. Clinical inputs are read
only from paths outside the repository tree and are never committed.

Third-party data: src/meshforge/data/strength_v0.csv and strength_v0_donors.csv
are derived from "Dataset on cadaveric human abdominal aorta aneurysm
biomechanics (uniaxial) and histology" by Gomes VC, da Silva ES, da Silva LF,
Gomes J, Raghavan ML, Silvestre G, Queiroz A, Marques M, Zyngier SP and
Chung TK-J, Mendeley Data, version 3 (2020), doi:10.17632/x64srrc39p.3,
licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The values
were changed (unit conversion, recomputation, flags); see
src/meshforge/data/STRENGTH_V0_SOURCES.md. These files are not covered by the
Apache License.

Demo scan (not in this repository; attached to the GitHub release v2.0.0 as
ct.nii.gz): subject s1364 of the TotalSegmentator dataset, Wasserthal et al.,
doi:10.5281/zenodo.10047292, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It is redistributed unchanged.

Programs the demo calls at run time. None of them is bundled in this
repository; each is installed separately and keeps its own licence:
- TotalSegmentator (Wasserthal et al., Apache-2.0): outlines the aorta on the CT.
- gmsh: fills the thrombus and the blood lumen with tetrahedra.
- CalculiX: solves the wall stress.
- OpenFOAM: solves the blood flow.
- vtk.js, served from the installed trame-vtk package: draws the 3-D view
  in the browser.
